          "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production orthographic four-view reference for a locally generated Hunyuan3D game environment mesh. Create ONE consistent solid ruined sandstone shrine-wall module for a Chinese-inspired desert roguelike FPS. Architecture: substantial thick ochre sandstone masonry, an asymmetric broken stepped top, a broad central shallow arched NICHE carved into a solid wall (no full-through doorway), weathered carved sun-disk relief inside the niche, two low projecting buttresses, a short surviving wing wall returning backward at one side. Compact massive connected silhouette, roughly 4.8 m wide, 4.4 m tall, 2.6 m deep. A few attached rubble chunks at the foot, realistic erosion and worn bevels, faded indigo and terracotta in the carving. Thick sculptural depth visible from left and right. No trees, cloth, characters, props detached from the main module, ground plane, landscape, magical effects, text or view labels. Style: high quality stylized game-ready PBR sculpture, crafted large-scale shapes, sculpted medium details, readable without tiny grain, dry matte stone. Composition: a wide white-background reference sheet with four isolated orthographic renders of THE SAME module in a single row ordered FRONT, LEFT, BACK, RIGHT. Equal physical scale and same ground baseline, all silhouettes fully visible with generous white gutters; sides must clearly show the 2.6m thickness and returning wall. Cameras level, strictly orthographic, no three-quarter views or perspective distortion. Neutral soft studio lighting with minimal shadows, white featureless background. Preserve all architectural details consistently between views. The whole image should be a clean 3D reconstruction input, not an illustrated scene.",
